From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] libgcc: strong gthread references on powerpc64-ps3-elf

With --enable-threads=posix, libgcc's gthr-posix.h refers to the pthread
functions weakly and treats a linked pthread_cancel as the sign that
threads are in use.  Weak references do not pull members out of static
archives, so a program whose only pthread user is libgcc (raw lv2
threads, no direct pthread call) could run the unwinder's object
registration without its lock.  librt implements pthreads and is on every
link (LIB_LV2_SPEC), so build libgcc with GTHREAD_USE_WEAK=0:
__gthread_active_p is always true, as libstdc++'s os/newlib configuration
already makes it for C++ code.

diff --git a/libgcc/config.host b/libgcc/config.host
index 5210576..26d7e1f 100644
--- a/libgcc/config.host
+++ b/libgcc/config.host
@@ -1269,7 +1269,7 @@ powerpc-*-rtems*)
 	extra_parts="$extra_parts crtbeginS.o crtendS.o crtbeginT.o ecrti.o ecrtn.o ncrti.o ncrtn.o"
 	;;
 powerpc64-ps3-elf*)
-	tmake_file="${tmake_file} rs6000/t-savresfgpr rs6000/t-ps3-crtstuff"
+	tmake_file="${tmake_file} rs6000/t-savresfgpr rs6000/t-ps3-crtstuff rs6000/t-ps3-gthreads"
 	;;
 powerpc64-ps3-kernel-elf*)
 	tmake_file="${tmake_file} rs6000/t-savresfgpr rs6000/t-ps3-crtstuff"
diff --git a/libgcc/config/rs6000/t-ps3-gthreads b/libgcc/config/rs6000/t-ps3-gthreads
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b4dd3dc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libgcc/config/rs6000/t-ps3-gthreads
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# libgcc thread-support flags for the PS3 LV2 PPU target.
+#
